<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "@id": "https://www.patronaccounting.com/accounting-bookkeeping-services/#faq",
  "datePublished": "2026-07-24T08:00:00+05:30",
  "dateModified": "2026-07-24T08:00:00+05:30",
  "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "Where should I start if several things are broken at once?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Start with the page matching the most urgent pain, usually pending books or reconciliations, and tell us the rest on the discovery call. We sequence the work: stabilise compliance first, clear backlog second, then set the monthly rhythm. You do not need to diagnose yourself perfectly; the directory just gives you a door to walk through."}},{"@type": "Question", "name": "How do you price a bundle drawn from different parts of this directory?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Plans across this hub start from ₹2,499/month (excl. GST and govt. charges); each service page lists its own starting fee. When you combine bookkeeping and accounting work across categories, we quote one consolidated monthly figure plus fixed fees for any one-time projects, all in writing before anything starts."}},{"@type": "Question", "name": "What does the first month look like after we sign?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Week one is access and setup: software, portals, banks and a chart of accounts review. Weeks two to four run the first full cycle with tighter checking than usual, ending with your first reporting pack and a call to correct anything that does not fit how you work. From month two the rhythm is standard."}},{"@type": "Question", "name": "Can a migration or catch-up project run alongside monthly work?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes, and that is the normal pattern. One-time projects run on their own timeline with a defined finish line, while the monthly engagement protects live due dates in parallel. Because both are staffed from one team, the project\\u2019s output lands directly in the monthly workflow instead of being thrown over a wall."}},{"@type": "Question", "name": "Is there anything these engagements deliberately do not cover?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Statutory audit must be performed by independent auditors; we prepare the books and coordinate the audit. Formal representation before tax authorities is scoped case by case when a matter arises. And we do not sell software licences; we configure and run what you own. Everything else across this directory is delivered in-house by our CA & CS team."}},{"@type": "Question", "name": "How is access managed when we use you for more than one service?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "One access grant covers the engagement, however many services you combine. Rights are role-based and limited to your named team, credentials sit in controlled vaults, and activity is reviewable. Adding a service adds scope, not another set of people holding your logins, and every team member signs confidentiality undertakings."}},{"@type": "Question", "name": "Do different industries get different teams or tools?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "The delivery backbone is one team working on your existing platform, whether that is Tally, Zoho Books, QuickBooks, Xero or Odoo. Industry pages change the checklists and reports applied, such as settlement reconciliations for marketplace sellers or fund-based reporting for trusts, not the people or the software. That is what keeps combined engagements coherent."}}]
}
